Phase 5c: Separate backend-neutral RHI objects from OpenGL realization
  Depends on 5b's execution/ownership contracts.
  Authority: Rendering.GpuCommands.Proposal.md, sections Shader and pipeline objects and Immediate execution and recorded lists;
    Rendering.GpuCommands.Contracts.md, sections Executable and pipeline contracts, Submission and failure rules, and Steady-state source ownership.
  Outcome: semantic objects do not depend on the concrete backend or carry OpenGL execution policy.

  ☑ Design the final ownership of backend realization data and originating-context admission for fixed
    objects and result-bearing operations. Distinguish backend-neutral description/identity/lifetime from
    native application state. Preserve the existing resource hierarchy and manager associations;
    do not invent parallel native owners or registry entries for purely managed pipelines.
  ☑ Remove OpenGLBackend fields, constructor requirements and concrete-backend context checks from
    RHIComputePipeline and RHIGraphicsPipeline. Move native graphics relevance, restoration footprint
    and other OpenGL realization data to backend-owned implementation state behind the agreed contract.
    Preserve fixed shader generation, description equality, independent disposal and submission guards.
  ☑ Apply the same separation to RHIPendingShaderCreation, RHIReadbackTicket and RHIQueryTicket,
    and inspect RHIShader and the remaining RHI object/reference types for equivalent dependencies.
    Preserve pending/ready/failure/cancellation, staging ownership, original-context cleanup and diagnostics.
  ☑ Make RHICommandContext use its backend-neutral execution contract for ordinary and owner-authorized
    operations, including mapping. Isolate concrete OpenGL selection/construction and native retirement
    notifications at the composition/integration boundary. Remove casts and the general-purpose OpenGL
    escape property; exact native engine integration must have an explicit, restricted final entry point.
  ☑ Migrate CloudSimpleGeometry, EngineFullscreenGeometry and EngineLiquidPoolGeometry off direct
    OpenGL.NativeOrigin and StateCache vertex-configuration epoch access. Keep engine layout/ownership
    and callback borrow policy in the adapters; use 5b's integration certification for context and native
    configuration validity. Preserve upload/adoption, replacement and original-context retirement together.
  ☑ Resolve the inherited EngineGraphicsGeometryTests imported-configuration failures and the
    EngineLiquidPoolGeometryTests index-association failure while migrating certification consumers.
    Preserve original-association and configuration checks; do not relax them to make draw fixtures pass.
  ☑ Test unchanged fixed-generation behavior, wrong-context rejection, recursive execution/retirement,
    shader/pipeline replacement failure, result completion/cancellation and context loss without exposing
    concrete backend implementation types to semantic callers.

