    shared setup/compact assertion qualification in 10.4 and family-wide assertion migration in 10.5
    are complete. Existing qualification corrections have a commit checkpoint in 10.6; redundant shader
    recompilation is addressed in 10.7. Subphase 10.8 separates the subsequent correction batch for review;
    10.9 identifies and designs changes to the remaining measured costs before implementation units are
    defined. Final combined correctness and test-runtime acceptance belong to 10.10. Earlier cleanup
    receipts do not demonstrate that the full suite became faster.

