  Analysis for discussion (source snapshot: working tree after the accepted 10.1 boundary)

    Scope and evidence:
    - Inspected the VGE project's source inventory, case attributes, native-fixture/trait references,
      filesystem operations, readback sites and shared fixture call paths. There are 961 C# files;
      788 contain Fact/Theory attributes after removing comments, with 3,324 attribute declarations.
      These are source counts, not discovered cases: partial classes, MemberData and InlineData expand
      differently. Of those files, 478 are under GPU and 310 elsewhere; directory placement alone does
      not establish classification. No build, test execution or new timing study supports this analysis.
    - The family partition below is exhaustive for those 478 GPU files. Apply its selectors in listed
      order, using the basename without extension; the final row owns every remaining GPU case file.
      Partial-class files remain with their family. Helpers/fixtures inherit every consuming family's
      contract, including support files outside GPU/Fixtures, GPU/Helpers and Helpers.
    - Existing source/receipts in 10.1 describe an accepted work boundary, not combined qualification.
      GPU.IntegrationTestPerformance.RemainingCosts.md and GPU.IntegrationTestPerformance.Analysis.md
      provide historical leads, not a current baseline or controlling benchmark requirement. The former's
      d9e46b0a run took about 21 minutes for 1,966 cases; that is not today's inventory or passing receipt.
      Its LumOnUniformTests repetition no longer exists, depth-oracle loops are already localized,
      lifecycle reload matrices are already reduced, and TestUniformRing already fences reused storage.
    - Controlling requirements: this plan's Phase 10/10.2 and Rendering.GpuCommands.Proposal.md
      (representative outcomes/verification); Rendering.GpuCommands.Contracts.md (Submission and failure
      rules, resource completion); Rendering.GpuResources.md (ownership and snapshot/change publication);
      Rendering.ShaderBindingState.md (Verification boundary). Retain values/tolerances, original resource
      identity, delivered changes, owner intervals, native effects and real completion. Historical links
      to the removed BindingAdmission proposal resolve through Git commit 46cbe4d2; they do not authorize
      reconstructing that temporary document. Current contracts govern the resulting implementation.

    Complete family coverage and intended disposition:
    - The selected design is full-domain compact GPU validation for every existing multi-texel content
      assertion, including arrays returned through fixtures/helpers and then scanned by callers. Keep
      current target dimensions, parameter rows, selected mip/region/layer and spatial coverage. Existing
      single-texel/tuple assertions remain direct small reads. This resolves the alternatives in the
      original task: no target shrinking or sparse replacement of whole-domain contracts is proposed.
      The table describes which predicates survive, not permission to choose weaker sampled coverage.
    - Readback dimensions are owner-derived, including runtime/capture-dependent extents: a full 2D mip
      transfers max(1,W>>m)*max(1,H>>m)*C*b bytes; arrays retain layer count, 3D images additionally retain
      max(1,D>>m), and cube selections retain all asserted faces. A region retains the exact requested
      width*height*depth*C*b; buffers retain their requested byte interval. C/b follow the readback format
      and component width, not necessarily storage format. Rgba float is 16 bytes/texel, R32f four.
      The new result is bounded counters/extrema/first-failure data, independent of those image extents.
      Examples: cloud rank storage is 32*256*4 = 32,768 bytes; depth reduction checks every mip of the
      existing 65x37 through 257x131 and 1xN/Nx1/odd test domains; stored-cloud views include
      1920x1080/3440x1377; surface checks cover every requested physical-page region and directional atlas
      layer. Imported capture widths/heights/layers/mips come from its validated manifest, not a guessed
      fixed resolution. Preserve these dimensions in the compact checks rather than download/scan them.

    | Family / ordered selector / case-bearing files | Existing coverage and preparation | Proposed coverage-preserving work; coverage retained |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | Diagnostic/mixed: Measurement or Performance in basename; BloomRadialDiagnostics, AoMinimumChildProduction, WaterBoundaryCapture / 14 | Timed repeated draws/dispatches, query completion, captured inputs and optional exports; some methods also assert correctness. | Separate diagnostic methods from ordinary correctness selection. Retain bounds, shader behavior and state assertions in correctness cases. Keep requested diagnostic output outside routine test execution; no elapsed-time oracle or automatic case deletion. Mixed AoMinimumChildProduction and WaterBoundaryCapture remain correctness owners for their non-measurement methods. |
    | SPIR-V: Spirv* / 2 | SpirvInventoryTests.BuiltVariantSpecializes, DeclaredGraphicsCombinationLinks, ComputeAssignmentsLinkAndRepresentativeDisposalPreservesReplacement; SpirvGraphicsLifecycleTests.RuntimeAssignmentsValidateAndRepresentativesRetirePreviousExecutable. | Retain every distinct packaged binary specialization, stage combination and production runtime-interface assignment. Raw linking does not replace production admission. Retain representative reload/retirement, invalid binary and working-generation preservation. Share immutable bytes/catalog only; do not remove the remaining full assignment matrix or replace it with CPU catalog enumeration. |
    | Atmosphere/sky: Atmosphere*, Celestial*, SunDisk*, MoonDisk*, Sky*, ProductionSky* / 21 | LUT/scattering computations, solar/lunar raster, orientation, lighting/publication and native sky integration; component programs and some full startup. | Consolidate identical program setup only for immutable numerical subjects. Replace full LUT/cube/color downloads with compact whole-domain finite/range/expected-value checks. Preserve horizon/zenith/disk edges, dark/bright limits, directional faces, publication/resize/replacement and production sky wiring. AtmosphereGpuScatteringTests and AtmosphereEngineBindingTests remain distinct numerical versus integration contracts. |
    | Clouds: Cloud* / 14 | Storage/compute, traversal/reduction, temporal freshness, blue-noise ranks, native simple-cloud draws and stored-volume view, including 1920x1080 and 3440x1377 targets. | CloudStoredVolumeViewTests/Fixtures/CloudStoredVolumeViewScene: retain odd extents, tail groups, viewport, temporal and large-size dispatch/coverage contracts with compact results. CloudBlueNoiseTextureTests.MasksHaveCompleteRanksAndStableOwnedStorage must retain all ranks for each of eight 32x32 slices and distinct slices, plus ownership/disposal; use rank occurrence counts and slice mismatch results. A sampled texel cannot prove the permutation. Retain density/diffuse/direct/reduction and observed native adapter effects separately. |
    | Liquids: Water*, Liquid*, Oit*, PhotometricCameraWater* / 28 | Real depth, refraction/composition, layer transport, OIT arithmetic, pool submission, lifecycle/state; WaterRefractionTests has optional binary overrides and export/timing branches. | Share immutable program preparation across compatible numerical inputs; replace multi-texel downloaded MRT images with whole-domain compact checks. Existing local shoreline/boundary tuples remain direct small reads. Retain full quality/compatibility contracts, foreground/above-water rejection, shoreline continuity, half-resolution interpolation and read budgets, energy/medium/blend/depth behavior. Keep WaterRefractionCaptureStateTests and WaterRefractionResolutionTests failures recorded in 10.1 as unresolved qualification items, not redundant assertions. Do not change expected exception types or tolerances to make them pass. |
    | LumOn/scene/probes: Surface*, LumOn*, Lumon*, WorldProbe*, SharedTrace*, SharedGeometry*, NearField*, ExpandedTrace*, TraceGeometry* / 111 | Component trace/filter/SH/gather/temporal tests and full worker/publication/lighting consumers; repeated frame observation and substantial atlas/history transfers. | SurfaceLightingConsumerRuntimeFixture.Frame/Energy/WaitObservations, SurfaceCacheRuntimeFixture.LightingObservations, SurfaceLightingRefreshSynchronization.CompleteConsumers and their callers: compact finite/energy/weight/confidence checks, device-side previous-history comparison and exact requested-page regions. Preserve every requested directional texel, exact history equality where asserted, fresh publication versus stale positive energy, retries, partial coverage, origin shifts and worker completion. Retain representative real startup/consumer/exit scenarios; component tests cannot replace those. Reuse already retained within-test programs, not a new global mutable cache. |
    | PBR/material/terrain: Terrain*, Material*, Microfacet*, Pbr*, PhotometricMaterial*, PhotometricLighting* / 39 | Terrain raster/tessellation/relief/temporal cases, BRDF/material energy, normal/depth bake, Poisson/multigrid and material atlas; real draws/dispatches. | Compact independently expected-value comparisons over existing domains; keep independent CPU numerical oracles and current tolerances. Preserve seams, triangle orientation, depth bias, odd/tail texels, convergence/residuals, atlas pages, replacement and installed production shader coverage. PbrPoisson* whole-domain residuals cannot become a center-pixel assertion. Keep full-chain bake/composition cases distinct from isolated numerical kernels. |
    | Postprocess/depth: AmbientOcclusion*, DepthHierarchy*, Camera*, ColorGrading*, Bloom*, LocalExposure*, LightShaft*, Postprocessing*, FinalDisplay*, PackedComposite*, Exposure* / 22 | Exposure/history/HDR, AO horizons/integrals, bloom/local exposure, conservative depth mips and renderer integration. | DepthHierarchyPassTests.EveryMipMatchesIndependentConservativeReduction/RepeatedFramesReuseCounterAndResizeStorage: retain all mip/odd/1xN/Nx1/1x1/last-group coverage with independent expected arrays and compact comparisons. Preserve AO foreground/background and horizon negatives, exposure history/photometry and adaptation at existing extents. Keep DepthHierarchyRendererTests routing/enablement distinct from reduction math. |
    | Engine/composition: SceneColor*, ClientRendering*, GBuffer*, FrameLighting*, FrameShader*, Engine*, NativeFrame*, NativeFog*, LightingResource*, DirectLighting*, OwnedPostprocess* / 38 | Engine target/binding scopes, shaders, boundary restoration, framebuffer rebuilds, ordered runtime composition and resource lifetime. | Retain real production entry points and observable output/state/restoration. Share immutable assets only; mock API dependencies not under test. Replace multi-texel output scans with compact assertions without reducing scope to call counts. ClientRenderingCompositionTests and engine boundary cases keep world/resize/reload/retirement distinctions. Full shader registration remains in representative startup scenarios. |
    | Remaining GPU files: RHI/resources/state/shader / 189 | Native creation, reference/metadata publication, context/name reuse, query/fence/mapping, bindless, interception, buffers, render passes, shader inputs/link/cache and state suppression. | Retain unique API/overload/native-effect and failure/restoration coverage. Reduce readback-API payloads to the smallest values proving format/stride/mip/layer/aspect/range; other output checks follow compact/selected-value rules. Distinguish static description equality from real admission and lifecycle. Keep exact once-only native forwarding, stale/context/name identity, completion, retention and error paths. No blanket matrix deletion: a distinct intercepted signature or resource lifecycle is not duplicated merely because the expected value matches. |

    Non-GPU-directory coverage (all 310 other case-bearing files):
    - Unit/Cache (6), Unit/Collections (1), Unit/Imaging (2), Unit/LumOn (65), Unit/Noise (2),
      Unit/Numerics (1), Unit/PBR (28), Unit/Rendering (52), Unit/Voxels (3), Unit/WorldPartition (8),
      the 19 files directly under Unit, and 123 root files: retain CPU contracts and parameter rows unless
      an exact equivalent is established. These cover caches/configuration, numeric/collection behavior,
      scheduling/admission/partitioning, scene/material decisions, shader source/contracts, patch routing,
      debug views, state values and lifecycle selection. No readback calls were found in these files.
      This does not imply no native setup: GraphicsPipelineDescriptionTests, GraphicsStateRelevanceTests
      and ConfigurableRasterizerDescriptionTests construct real shaders through HeadlessGLFixture.
      Split genuinely pure subcases only if they can use legal descriptions without fabricated ready
      references; native admission and shader-dependent cases stay GPU integration tests.
    - Mixed GPU/ShaderDefineInjectionTests.Shader source-map/import case (Fact at line 131): migrate the
      CPU preprocessor/source-map assertions to the CPU source-test family using immutable built sources.
      Keep source IDs/import locations, remove File.Exists-based success-by-skip and physical include scans.
      Preserve relative include identity rather than flattening unrelated include paths to filenames.
    - The existing CPU state collection and 10.1 trait moves already isolate global CPU/Harmony state.
      Retain these; do not require OpenGL initialization just to serialize stateful CPU tests. Preserve
      NearFieldMaterialCaptureCollection's DisableParallelization boundary as well as GPU serialization.

    Filesystem mapping (direct sites and the exercised storage/asset call paths):
    - Already in memory: Unit/Cache/DiskBlobCacheStoreTests, DiskJsonDictionaryCacheStoreTests,
      DebouncedMetaWritesTests, DataCacheSystemTests; Unit/Rendering/ProgramBinaryStoreTests;
      GPU/DriverProgramCacheTests, ShaderDigestIndexCacheTests, ShaderAssetCandidateTests and
      ShaderLinkBatchTests pass CountingDiskCacheFileSystem into the actual stores. Material-atlas
      fixtures use InMemoryMaterialAtlasFileSystem; asset proxies use TestAssetSnapshot/ShaderAssetFileSystem.
      Retain real serialization, atomic-replacement protocol, concurrent access, corruption/truncation,
      reload and failure assertions against providers. Do not recreate these subjects as physical I/O tests
      or describe provider tests as OS atomicity proof. No second mock filesystem abstraction is needed.
      At analysis time HeadlessGLFixture.EnsureContextValid set DriverProgramCache.Bypass=true so ordinary
      preparation could not fall through to physical cache storage. That blanket bypass is superseded by
      the approved 10.7 design: enable the existing cache by default against an in-memory provider, with
      explicit suite-level opt-outs and isolated stores for cache subjects. Preserve I/O isolation and
      restore scoped cache policy explicitly; enabling the default must not reach physical cache storage.
    - Remaining direct source reads: GPU/ShaderDefineInjectionTests as above; GPU/Fixtures/
      CapturedAmbientOcclusionFixture reads manifest.json and payload bytes. Snapshot explicitly requested
      captures once through a provider, preserving manifest dimensions/formats/mips, digest and malformed-
      input checks. Capture-driven evaluation is an opt-in diagnostic workload, not a default asset source.
    - Helpers/TestAssetSnapshot.LoadBuilt reads fixture-inputs.txt and the explicit build-owned
      files once; its directory-taking constructor can enumerate. Routine callers should use the manifest
      snapshot and independent in-memory overlays. Required shader bytes, schemas, contract baselines,
      config patches and installed-engine source copies are immutable build inputs, not cache persistence.
      Tests must not silently discover stale output or access the live game asset tree. The csproj owns
      freezing/copying those inputs; build/runner I/O is distinct from repeated test-body I/O.
    - GPU/Fixtures/EngineDependencyResolution and RHIContractIsolationTests.Execution read/probe required
      assemblies (the latter caches its PE reference). Preserve loader/compiler inputs; mocks cannot
      replace a real assembly while retaining the assembly-boundary subject. No test-owned persistence.
    - GPU/LumOnDebugShaderDemandTimingTests explicitly opens a physical ProgramBinaryStore and removes its
      directory. Split correctness/demand/cache expectations onto the existing in-memory provider; retain
      optional profiling as a diagnostic entry point outside ordinary correctness execution. No physical
      cache experiment is required for this plan's acceptance.
    - Export/input-override sites: root AtmosphereTensorMeasurementTests and
      AtmosphereMultipleScatteringTensorMeasurementTests; GPU/BloomRadialDiagnosticsTests,
      AoMinimumChildProductionTests, AmbientOcclusionPerformanceTests, MicrofacetEnergyMeasurementTests,
      TerrainDetailMeasurementTests, SurfaceWorkDiagnosticMeasurementTests,
      SurfaceUpdateBudgetMeasurementTests, WorldProbeRoutingMeasurementTests; GPU/Helpers/
      FramebufferBmpCapture; GPU/WaterBoundaryCaptureTests and WaterRefractionTests.
      Separate optional binary/capture providers and export sinks from retained correctness assertions;
      ordinary VGE tests use memory, including export formatting/failure tests. Filesystem exporters, if
      kept for manual diagnosis, are explicit utilities rather than returning passing tests when disabled.
      The 19 files with direct File/Directory signals include these exporters, bootstrap/assembly inputs,
      the physical timing cache and the two source/capture readers; this is not 19 unmocked storage subjects.

    Shared setup, consolidation and removal decisions:
    - GPU/Fixtures/RuntimeLightingPrograms.Initialize registers every production program. Keep this for
      startup/registration, full runtime and replacement subjects; use ComponentShaderPrograms.Create/
      CreateCompute/CreateDepthHierarchy for isolated numerical/component tests. A failed unused program
      must not disable an unrelated component case. Shared binaries/catalogs/expected CPU data may be
      immutable; GPU programs and native objects stay with an explicit context-bound fixture owner.
    - GPU/Fixtures/LayeredTestTexture.Create currently downloads source textures, broadcasts/resamples CPU
      arrays and uploads again. Replace equal-size, format-compatible construction with GPU copies; use authored CPU
      data for constant fixtures, explicit GPU copy/blit for required resampling. Retain layer identity,
      precision, zero-filled missing channels and sampling semantics. Format conversion needs explicit
      channel expansion; do not replace it with an incompatible raw copy or change nearest sampling into interpolation.
    - GPU/Fixtures/RenderTestBase.EnsureContextValid invalidates all state and drains GetError even for
      nested target/draw/read helpers. Remove routine blanket purges/error swallowing under the established
      interception invariant. Use named initialization/context-retirement/fault-injection boundaries and
      meaningful error assertions that report earlier failures. Preserve restoration after deliberate
      native bypasses. Review HeadlessGLFixture, ShaderTestFramework, LumOnShaderFunctionalTestBase and their disposal
      scopes together; no unsupported assumption that every reset or error query is unnecessary.
    - TestUniformRing.BeginFrame/RetireSubmittedWork already uses an originating-context fence before
      resetting its persistent page. Retain this independent of assertion readback. Keep map/query/ticket
      and driver failure completion; remove Finish/Flush only where the following synchronous operation
      already supplies the entire required ordering. Never use GL.Finish as universal test cleanup.
    - Candidate consolidation units are numerical cases with the same immutable program/target contract
      within each family above. Keep named theory rows and independent resets; no megatest depending on
      prior rows. Full registration, reload, creation, lifetime and context-switch subjects keep fresh
      owners. No further case deletion is justified by this analysis: matching names/results alone do not
      prove redundancy. Remove superseded helper paths and duplicate setup/observations only when their
      exact assertions have moved. Existing 10.1 reductions are retained, not counted again as new work.

    Readback and instrumentation design:
    - Keep existing single-texel/local tuple assertions and their controlled targets. All multi-texel content contracts use
      a fixture-owned generic GPU comparison/reduction with only bounded counters/extrema/first-failure
      coordinates returned: nonfinite counts, independent expected-value mismatch, range/energy/confidence
      and history equality. Preserve actual domains: 2D, layered/3D/cube selections, integer/depth aspects,
      mips and channel masks. Keep CPU-authored expected data; do not replicate production BRDF, tracing,
      reduction or filtering algorithms in the checker. Exact comparison must deliberately cover signed
      zero, NaN/infinity and subnormals; tolerance remains the existing assertion's tolerance.
    - Surface histories need full-domain previous GPU snapshots, not a few sampled texels. Readiness checks
      retain requested-page coverage, alpha/sample weights and publication freshness, not just a positive
      sum. Shader read-count/dispatch counter assertions remain workload contracts, never output oracles.
      Failure-only diagnostic dumps are separate from required finite/energy checks and normal readback.
    - Do not adopt TestResults/GpuTests101/deferred-gpu-assertions as implemented machinery. Its cached raw
      names use thread-local state-cache identity rather than physical context identity; SSBO base/range
      restoration, partial construction, exact-float and native failure reporting need redesign. Prefer
      copies for fixture input construction; introduce only the generic checker operations needed above.
      Give its programs/buffers explicit original-context ownership, assert sentinel/result validity and
      preserve pack/program/generic and indexed binding state. No global native-name cache or success on
      failed dispatch. Cover exception cleanup and context switches before using it as another oracle.
    - GPU/Fixtures/NativeDriverCapture and NativeIndexedDrawCapture catch callback exceptions and rethrow
      after native return/cleanup. Retain this required unmanaged-boundary containment and exactly-once
      forwarding/restored slots; it is not swallowed failure. GraphicsTransitionCapture intentionally
      injects GetError results for negative restoration tests. LegacyFixedFunctionReference is a historical
      negative-control oracle, not a replacement production state path. Retain both where their assertion
      needs them. Reflection into scheduler/query state is eligible for removal only with an equivalent
      existing observable fixture seam; do not add broad production inspection APIs or weaken freshness.

    Approved execution boundaries (10.3–10.5 and final qualification in 10.10 below):
    1. Finish execution classification and I/O isolation: Category=GpuIntegration remains the native test
       category and collection GPU stays serial. Keep UnitTests.runsettings's native exclusion and add
       Purpose=Diagnostic to diagnostic methods, excluded from routine unit/GPU correctness runs.
       Explicit diagnostic commands select Purpose=Diagnostic; correctness commands exclude that value.
       Scenario=HeadlessRuntime describes actual production runtime execution, not filenames containing
       Runtime. Split mixed methods; avoid project/directory renames without a concrete execution benefit.
       Reconcile the test csproj, both runsettings and documented commands; no old Category=GPU command.
    2. Fix shared setup/state/copy infrastructure and design/qualify the minimal compact assertion fixture.
       Keep immutable asset sharing separate from per-context GPU owners and per-test mutable subjects.
    3. Migrate atlas/history/runtime consumers together, preserving mandatory wait observations and exact
       history/freshness contracts; migrate the numerical/spatial families using the coverage table.
       Keep API readback subjects minimal and independent from the checker consuming them.
    4. Reconcile all retained/remapped cases, documentation and filters; delegated focused checks for each
       affected unit, then one complete VGE correctness suite on the combined source, Debug/Release where
       required by the parent contract. Record actual counts/failures/skips and available runner durations.
       Diagnose the outstanding water-state failures; do not loosen assertions. Native checks establish
       headless behavior only. User-run visual acceptance and unrelated tool projects remain separate.
       Review/remove TestResults/GpuTests101/deferred-gpu-assertions/ and tracked-candidate.patch after
       preserving decisions/useful evidence; retain authoritative plans, proposals and qualification TRX/logs.
    Review: source census and mappings received a second review and independent completion audit;
      no build/test run was needed for this analysis. The user subsequently approved the design and
      execution boundaries, including independently expected full-domain GPU checks with compact results.
      The original implementation boundaries map to 10.3–10.5 and 10.10; the user subsequently added the
      existing-work checkpoint in 10.6 and default-enabled shader caching in 10.7. The second review and
      independent completion audit of the original analysis passed; 10.2 is complete. Only this planning
      document changed; no runtime/test implementation, staging, commit or new performance evidence is
      part of this analysis boundary.
      Coverage not explicitly replaced above stays intact.

