    Complete assertion-route cost inventory (source sites, not runtime frequencies):
    - The comparison/predicate/reduction routes reach GpuImageAssertions.Run: fresh result image (128 bytes), initialized histogram
      (4 bytes ordinary, 16,384 bytes statistics, rank-domain size for CheckRanks), optional dummy expected
      image, uniform/binding/state setup, dispatch/barriers and synchronous 128-byte result read. All ordinary
      source observations allocate/copy a full selected GpuImageSnapshot first; correlated routes copy each
      source. Cached executable bytes do not eliminate a new program installation in each new checker owner.
    - The ordinary kernel globally atomically increments visit/component/positive/nonzero counters and
      extrema for successful texels/components. This creates shared-counter contention even without failures.
      Statistics adds fixed 256-group and final reductions after the ordinary pass; ranks add a histogram
      validation pass. Individual stage costs are not isolated; bounded whole-helper timings are measured
      below. Net benefit over the former complete CPU assertions remains unknown, especially for tiny domains.

    | Route | CPU preparation / upload beyond the common work | Selected disposition |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | Compare / CompareBits | Caller array; Compare adds a full float-to-uint copy, then RGBA-padded uint packing; 16 bytes/texel uploaded even for scalar sources. Additive-layer mode also snapshots its reference. | Replace regular constants/patterns with compact expectations; retain independent numerical/native bit arrays where justified. |
    | CompareDouble | Finite scan plus low/high packing; 32 bytes/texel uploaded, apart from caller doubles. | Keep necessary CPU numerical oracles; compact row/scenario tables where values repeat. |
    | CompareIntervals | Lower/upper validation and packing; 64 bytes/texel uploaded, apart from two caller double arrays and sliced copies. | Prefer independently authored bounds per scenario/row/region, preserving exact double values and intersections. |
    | CompareFloating | Expected/tolerance validation plus two RGBA uint layers; 32 bytes/texel uploaded. | Preserve float subtraction/tolerance semantics; compact per-scenario data where regular. |
    | CompareRgba8 | Full GPU decode projection plus extra snapshots; byte-to-float CPU copy then Compare's packing/upload. | Compare normalized metadata bytes directly in the existing checker, retaining rounding semantics. |
    | CompareSelected | Sparse dictionary expanded to full RGBA uint image, 16 bytes/texel uploaded. | Upload only nominated coordinate/value records; retain exact authored points and compared-component proof. |
    | WeightedStatistics | Independent CPU quadrature arrays, finite scan and double-pair packing; 16 bytes/texel uploaded. | Retain independent quadrature; cache immutable authored weights per exact domain or compact parameters only if independence/precision is preserved. |
    | PeriodicLaplacianResidual | CPU RHS padded to RGBA uint, 16 bytes/texel uploaded, plus three statistics dispatches. | Retain independent equation/RHS; avoid padding/reupload for unchanged authored RHS within its owner. |
    | PredicateAt | 16 bytes/nominated point coordinate upload; predicate snapshots domain and source. | Keep sparse authored-domain semantics; reuse the compact coordinate data within an explicit owner. |
    | Inspect, CompareConstant, CompareStencil, CountMatching, InspectCoverage, CompareChannelRatios, CountFlags | Compact scalar/vector parameters, no image-sized expected upload. | Retain generic operations, combine compatible checks and remove unrequested reduction work. |
    | Predicate | Authored source string/parameters, up to four source snapshots, kernel variant per distinct body. | Keep independent predicates; parameterize repeated bodies rather than specialize every value into source. |
    | CompareRelation, CountExcess, CompareHistory | Compact parameters; two/three snapshots or actual plus retained history. | Retain GPU histories; reuse each observation snapshot once within its valid interval. |
    | Statistics, OrderedFloatSum, Extremum, Brightest | Statistics may project squared values; ordered sum projects then reduces; extrema/brightest run multiple snapshots/checkers and finally a nominated tuple. | Preserve summation precision/order and selected witness; avoid duplicate passes/copies where the same result supplies multiple facts. |
    | CheckRanks | No CPU expected image; rank histogram and second complete rank-validation dispatch, including slice-difference witnesses. | Retain permutation/missing/duplicate/range proof and all slices; aggregate ordinary counters without removing the independent histogram check. |
    | GpuImageTransform / GpuLayerCopy / GpuImageSet / NativeFramebufferImage | Additional source snapshots, projection/copy storage and dispatches; histories intentionally retain immutable results. | Share observation captures within a completed epoch, preserve active-pass/format/aspect/restoration boundaries and history ownership. |
    | GpuLocalRead / direct nominated tuples | Small CPU result allocation/read; some paths first snapshot the selection. No full expected image or checker reduction. | Preserve local numerical/native observations; batch independent nominated tuples where compatible without turning them into whole-image readbacks. |

    Caller disposition inventory (basenames under VanillaGraphicsExpanded.Tests; partials/helpers included):
    - Regular authored expectations, migrate to compact constants/row/region/scenario records or independent
