Phase 10.9.2: Agree on focused observation boundaries and the coverage consolidation map
  Depends on the approved read-only audit and the accepted 10.9.1 checkpoint.
  Outcome: an agreed smaller architecture and explicit per-family keep/consolidate/simplify dispositions.
  Status: complete by explicit user approval on 2026-11-01. The design and coverage map below are agreed.
    This is a planning-only boundary. No runtime/helper changes, test deletion, build or test run is required.

  Approved observation architecture (not implemented):
    - HeadlessGLFixture explicitly owns comparison, reduction/statistics and selection/projection services.
      RenderTestBase and consuming fixtures receive these dependencies directly; no thread-static Current
      lookup, global registry, new scheduler, universal request dispatcher or new cache. Services own only
      observation machinery. Test cases continue to own fresh programs/resources when those are subjects.
    - Comparison operations accept separate typed requests for constant/region expectations, independent
      reference data, sparse coordinate/value records and retained-history equality. A shared image-domain
      value uses existing RHI subresource/region/aspect types plus numeric interpretation and channel mask;
      it does not duplicate resource metadata or own the source. Each request contains only its operation's
      inputs. Results expose completion, visited/compared counts, mismatch count and earliest failure with
      source coordinates/component and expected/actual values where meaningful. No overloaded counter slots
      or uncomputed fields presented as zeros. Witness predicates additionally require their witness count.
    - Reduction operations have separate count/range/extremum, double-moment/weighted-moment and ordered-float
      contracts. Requested facts determine work and typed results. Double multiplication versus float-square-
      then-double accumulation remains explicit. Ordered-float evaluation preserves expression grouping,
      traversal order and each float rounding; it produces one scalar rather than a full image of zeros.
      Workgroup aggregation applies only where it preserves the authored numerical contract. The existing
      statistics precision failure must be explained and fixed in 10.9.4, not accepted by widening tolerance.
    - Selection returns deterministic coordinates/value (first original linear index on ties). Preserve
      existing full-domain finite checks: any selected NaN/infinity rejects rather than being skipped;
      an empty/invalid domain cannot yield a valid candidate. Brightest retains its luminance expression and reads
      only the selected original tuple. Projection creates a genuinely required output/history image;
      scalar reductions do not masquerade as projections. Generic mechanics stay shared, while authored
      numerical predicates/projections live in their owning cloud/water/surface/etc. shader asset families.
      Group related policies by domain responsibility; avoid one infrastructure class/program per test or
      per expected value. Independent oracles cannot call the production algorithm they verify.
    - All checker executables remain declared, precompiled production assets loaded through the existing
      default in-memory test binary cache and production shader owners. Each service prepares only its
      required programs explicitly during ordinary test setup, before hostile selectors, active passes or
      native observation callbacks. First use inside those boundaries must not trigger compilation/loading.
      Retain owners through their original context/manager lifetime and retire them before those services;
      manager retirement invalidates old preparations. Preserve cache opt-outs and original thread/context
      rules. Failed preparation cleans partial owners and reports failure; no source-compiler fallback.
    - Immediate observation borrows an unchanged, completed source only until synchronous return. It issues
      no automatic source copy. The caller supplies correct producer synchronization/access transitions;
      the helper does not infer hazards. Retained-history capture explicitly owns an independent copy before
      later mutation/resize/retirement. An active attachment/native callback uses an explicit native copy at
      that observation boundary, then observes the copy outside the production pass. Do not widen the pass.
      Existing snapshots remain necessary where borrowing cannot preserve the original interpretation.
    - Every route retains exact mip, selected region, array/cube face or 3D Z range and represented channels.
      Compare stored sRGB bytes without accidental sampling decode. Packed stencil observation must not
      change the subject's depth/stencil mode; use an owned copy when needed. Integer/bitwise reads preserve
      all bits; normalized-byte reconstruction, NaN/infinity, signed-zero and subnormal policies follow each
      original oracle. Unsupported direct interpretations take an explicit copy/conversion route, never
      silent resampling. Multisample observation keeps its authored sample/resolve semantics.
    - Scratch belongs to its explicit service/context and is reused only after the preceding immediate
      operation completes. Reset result sentinels, counters, histogram/partials and logical inputs before
      every use, including after failure. Allocate only required capacity/resources; no dummy image or
      histogram for operations that do not use them. Release scratch before manager/context destruction.
      Native observation scopes preserve only selectors actually touched, including exact UBO base/range,
      pack and aspect state where relevant, on both success and exception. Do not repair production state
      or drain unrelated errors. RHI tests use independent native reads/captures for the behavior under test;
      production-backed checking is not proof of the same RHI transfer/binding operation it exercises.

  Approved route and cost decisions:
    | Authored observation | Selected route and preserved proof | Avoidable work / remaining cost |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | One scalar/tuple or a few named texels, including current water MRT outputs | Direct bounded native read and CPU assertion; exact coordinate/layer/format and independent expected tuple. | No checker dispatch/full-image snapshot/upload. Each immediate read may still synchronize; batching is deferred. |
    | Sparse nominated points in a large image | Typed integer coordinate/value or predicate records, dispatch only those points; retain duplicates/order if authored, every mask and exact compared count. | O(selected points) expectation/dispatch work, no dense expansion or enclosing source copy; retain small CPU reads when simpler. |
    | Substantial domain with uniform/regular expectations | GPU whole-domain comparison against constants, row/region tables or domain-owned independent predicates. | No repeated CPU expected pixels; requested comparison facts only, bounded result read, one immediate completion. |
    | Substantial domain with irreducible CPU numerical reference | Keep independently computed arrays/quadrature/double bounds and exact tolerance; explicit reference owner can reuse unchanged uploads. | Upload remains real work; avoid padding/duplicate bands but do not replace an independent oracle with the tested algorithm. |
    | History/temporal equality or mapped old/new domains | One explicitly owned pre-mutation capture; compare current borrowed domain to retained original with exact region mapping. | Required capture stays; remove nested captures of either unchanged image. No implicit cross-check snapshot cache. |
    | Counts, extrema, ranks, moments, ordered scalar | Dedicated requested-fact reduction, rank occurrence/slice checks or ordered scalar operation. Completion per required stage plus full selected-domain counts. | Workgroup count reduction avoids global per-component contention; no unused moments/extrema or full scalar intermediate. Preserve histogram and double/ordered arithmetic when required. |
    Costs to record separately during implementation: preparation and allocation, copied bytes, CPU reference
    construction/upload bytes, visited elements, dispatches/atomics, touched selector scopes and immediate
    completion waits. Reuse 10.9's bounded helper evidence with its stated limits. No speedup follows from
    bounded result size alone; no numerical acceptance threshold or new full baseline run is introduced.

