Phase 10.9.6: Compute only requested facts and reduce counters within workgroups
  Depends on 10.9.4–10.9.5. Replaces the former reduction 10.9.3; separate implementation/commit boundary.
  Outcome: pass/fail operations avoid unrelated statistics and global per-component contention.

  ☐ Select required facts explicitly. Ordinary equality need not calculate extrema, positivity, nonzero
    counts or moments unless consumed. Keep required visits/completion proof and failure diagnostics;
    result types must not expose uncomputed fields as valid zeros. Validate all surviving result consumers.
  ☐ Aggregate required counts, failures, extrema and earliest witness/failure coordinates within workgroups
    before global publication. Preserve exact integer/bit semantics, channel masks and selected regions;
    partial/tail invocations must participate safely in barriers without counting nonexistent components.
  ☐ Preserve missing/failed-dispatch sentinels and full selected-domain proof, histogram duplicate/missing
    ranks and slice differences. Do not weaken independent completion checks to save counter work.
  ☐ Keep ordered-float accumulation and existing double statistics contracts distinct from associative
    counter reductions. Remove full-domain intermediates/general moment passes used solely to retrieve
    one already-computed ordered scalar; preserve its expression grouping, rounding and traversal order.
    Never change tolerances, NaN/infinity/signed-zero/subnormal policies to fit a parallel algorithm.
  ☐ Delegate tiny/large/odd-tail, numeric-kind, overflow/domain-limit and negative completion checks;
    record requested work and resulting focused timings, then satisfy shared review/metrics acceptance.

