Final acceptance
  ☐ All eleven phases, their subphases and mandatory migration receipts are satisfied; later cleanup never substitutes for
    removing superseded APIs within their owning migration unit.
  ☐ Final APIs are backend-neutral, managed OpenGL execution requires 4.5, and every native operation has
    one execution owner with existing manager metadata/lifetime authority and preserved cache behavior.
  ☐ GraphicsCommandContext and StateCache's old execution/name surfaces are gone; shader/PSO, geometry,
    targets, uniforms, synchronization and recording follow the approved final contracts.
  ☐ Tests, current-state docs, package verification and user-run evidence support the claimed outcome
    without unsupported rendering-performance claims or treating headless results as visual acceptance.

Proposal coverage map
  Boundary, operations, capabilities and resource inputs: Phases 1–5; final cache split in Phase 7.
  Creation/adoption, initial content, original identity and retirement: Phases 2–5; corrections in 8; lifecycle tests in 6/9.
  Shader/PSO creation, generation identity, replacement and ownership: Phase 5; recorded rejection in 6.
  Geometry, attachment targets and immediate submission: Phase 5; recorded consumption in 6.
  Uniform capture, physical publication and history: Phase 5; recording/epoch/cancellation tests in 6.
  Recording, ownership transfer, tickets, failure and CPU/GPU completion: Phases 4/6.
  Dependency inversion for manager services, wrappers and semantic RHI objects: subphases 5b–5e and 8a–8j.
  Semantic buffer/shader/reflection schemas and authored resource types: subphase 8d.
  Manager operation guards, context discovery and backend-only boundary footprints: subphase 8f.
  Transitive schema isolation and intentional composition/native-payload boundary qualification: subphase 8j.
  Persistent state knowledge and removal of obsolete frame/resize/startup purges: subphase 8g.
  Native OpenTK dispatch, observational forwarding and remaining handler propagation: subphase 8h.
  Observer classification, generated safety plumbing, effect relevance and nonthrowing startup: subphase 8h.1.
  Complete creation interception and maintained lifecycle metadata with bounded acquisition: subphase 8i.
  RHI management-service naming and complete caller/documentation reconciliation: subphase 8k.
  Native dispatch, publication, exact integration and no-shim migration: mandatory receipts, Phases 2–8.
  Representative outcomes, efficient-execution checks, package and user-run qualification: Phase 9, supported
    by focused verification and current-state documentation in every owning migration unit.
  GPU integration-test classification, I/O isolation, coverage consolidation and compact assertions: Phase 10.
  Legacy test shader ownership and production submission, with justified native/oracle boundaries: Phase 11.

## Retained migration evidence

The temporary migration map was removed after its current contracts were reconciled into
Rendering.GpuResources.md (Snapshot and change publication), Rendering.GpuCommands.Contracts.md
(Resource completion) and Rendering.ShaderBindingState.md (Prepared executable bindings / Prepared
resource submission). Historical before/after inventories and exact older candidate commands remain
retrievable from Git blob 21185ed8770e73c1a8c43384f9138a9669bf53b6 at commit
24d01f73770a54fb64d0e861387290a249765b99. This immutable historical record is not a live controlling
document or qualification of later source. Existing per-unit receipts and limitations above remain.

Resource-change task/source/evidence traceability:

| Requirement | Final source route | Focused evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Equality, meaningful effects and all fourteen families | MetadataCollections; GpuTextureMetadata/GpuFramebufferMetadata/GpuProgramMetadata; GpuResourceMetadataEntry.Publish/Withdraw; RHIResourceChange | ResourceChangePublicationTests: structural equality/hash, initial/late/equal delivery, equal-descriptor replacements and fourteen-kind lifecycle matrix. |
| Facts before consumers; committed result survives callback failure | RHIResourceManager.ChangeDelivery, MetadataPublication, MetadataOperation, ProgramFields; AssignMetadataSnapshot and OnResourceChanged | CPU ordering/failure/reentry cases; ResourceChangeNativeTests committed-allocation failure and controlled-assignment exclusion. |
| Original backing and selected images | BufferTextureDependencies, RenderbufferTextureDependencies, DependencyAvailability, NativeTextureViews, OwnerImages | Source-only recovery versus independent child uncertainty, detached backing, reused names, native buffer/view/renderbuffer checks and explicit framebuffer owner events. |
| Revision and fixed realization readers | RHIGeometryImport/GeometryVertexArray configuration epochs; HasCommittedMetadata; pending link submitted revision; fixed local shader prepared-interface identity | Geometry lifecycle/import/interception, shader compatibility, executable lifecycle and local equal-interface replacement tests. |
| Lifetime/thread closure | Entry synchronization and idempotent terminal capture; original cleanup queue; context retirement | CPU queued-retirement/teardown/name reuse and foreign-thread rejection; native worker/local-image retirement. |

Canonical shader-enabled Debug and ordinary optimized Release builds passed with zero errors.
Each focused run passed 252/252 (52 CPU, 200 GPU), zero failures/skips, without JIT overrides.
Exact receipts: artifacts/resource-change-phase2-affinity-{debug,release}-build.log and
artifacts/TestResults/resource-change-phase2-affinity-{debug,release}.trx. Documentation-only closeout
leaves that runtime/test source unchanged. CPU cases establish manager semantics; GPU integration
cases establish native behavior, not live rendering, package identity or measured performance.

Parent 9.3 retains all final combined-suite, package and user acceptance work. Earlier 8,389-pass/
35-failure full-run candidates and candidate27 packaging remain historical; candidate34 focused
472/472 GPU and 256/256 shader-tool passes do not qualify the new combined runtime. Candidate35 was
stopped and supplies no complete-suite or final-package receipt. The unavailable historical
artifacts/phase8h/closure5-head-comparison.json was not recovered; the approved replacement is current
per-case full-suite evidence, retaining the original fourteen sequence-sensitive regression checks.
The removed RG-to-RGBA clear workaround remains absent: a passing focused recheck did not explain
earlier failures, and parent 9.3 retains diagnosis without an assumed driver defect. Optional external
producer imports, unsupported hardware paths and user-run appearance remain unqualified where not
executed. Phase 10 retains GPU integration terminology, I/O isolation/mocks, redundant-case removal,
coverage consolidation and compact assertions without bulk pixel readbacks.

### User-run visual and runtime checklist

Use the final qualified Release package; record its runtime DLL hash, game version, GPU/driver,
settings and actual results. No timing measurement or agent-launched game is required.

- [ ] Enter a world; inspect terrain, entities, sky, liquids and postprocessing for missing outputs,
  corrupt geometry, binding errors and incorrect lighting.
- [ ] Move along a shallow shoreline with lowest refraction quality and half-resolution backgrounds;
  check abrupt color steps and foreground leaks.
- [ ] Exercise configured atmosphere/exposure/depth/lighting compute consumers and inspect current results.
- [ ] Exercise cloud mode, terrain/liquid occlusion, enable/disable and movement for stale content.
- [ ] Resize window/render resolution and check replacement targets, aspect ratio, cloud/depth and postprocessing.
- [ ] Reload shaders/change shader settings; check compatible replacement and preservation on failure.
- [ ] Leave/reenter a world and shut down; check stale resources, disposal/context errors and late callbacks.

User evidence remains pending. Record failures with logs/reproduction; unexecuted hardware/import cases
remain unqualified. Headless tests and older installed binaries cannot check these boxes.
